    "Question #: 4": {
      "Title": "Exam 9A0-397 topic 1 question 4 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A DevOps engineer needs to install bundles via content packages for a continuous deployment setup."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "In which two ways should this be configured? (Choose two.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. The JCR installer will only update the bundle if the filename changes; always use a unique bundle version in the filename"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. For an out-of-the-box installation, bundles can be installed from /apps./libs and /etc"
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. To install bundles for a certain runmode only, the folder name can be used to limit environments where a bundle is installed"
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. Before the deployment of the new bundle, remove the old bundle from JCR as first deployment step to make sure the bundle is updated"
            }
          ]
        },
        "E": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "E. Whenever the JCR installer detects a change of a bundle file, it will install it to the Felix runtime"
            }
          ]
        },
        "F": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "F. The JCR installer detects bundle changes at arbitrary depths in the JCR tree and automatically deploys those changes bundles"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": []
      },
      "Explanation": {
